pref-hint = Leave the CLI path empty to find it automatically (SiYuan ships it as SiYuan-Kernel in the installation's resources/kernel folder). Leave the workspace empty to use the workspace SiYuan has open, and the notebook empty to use the first one.

pref-destination-title = Send to
pref-destination = Destination
pref-destination-daily = Today's daily note
pref-destination-document = A document
pref-destination-item = One document per item
pref-target-document = Document title or ID
pref-item-doc-name = Title of the new document (template variables work)
pref-item-doc-path = Parent path (for example /Reading)
pref-item-notes-subdocs = Put each child note into its own document under the item's document
pref-item-notes-subdocs-hint = With this on, “Sync this item” writes the information and abstract into the literature note and makes every Zotero child note a sub-document below it. A changed note is rewritten in place, and a deleted note takes its document with it. Turning it off writes the notes inline again and removes the sub-documents this plugin made.
pref-sent-action = An annotation that was already sent
pref-sent-action-ask = Ask me each time
pref-sent-action-skip = Skip it
pref-sent-action-send = Send another one
pref-sent-action-replace = Replace the last one
pref-destination-hint = The default is today's daily note. With “A document”, enter its title or block ID. With “One document per item”, the plugin creates a document for the item in the chosen notebook and remembers it with custom-zotero-item-key, so later notes go into the same one. This destination can have a template of its own: switch “Template for” in “Send template” below to “One document per item”. Saving a template also saves these destination settings, and loading it restores them.

pref-auto-title = Automatic sending and the queue
pref-auto-send = Send new annotations automatically
pref-auto-hint = Off by default. When it is on, only annotations that match every condition below are sent; a condition left empty, or with nothing ticked, means no restriction for that dimension.
pref-auto-colors = Colours
pref-auto-color-yellow = Yellow
pref-auto-color-red = Red
pref-auto-color-green = Green
pref-auto-color-blue = Blue
pref-auto-color-purple = Purple
pref-auto-color-magenta = Magenta
pref-auto-color-orange = Orange
pref-auto-color-gray = Gray
pref-auto-tags = Tags (comma-separated)
pref-auto-types = Annotation kinds
pref-auto-type-highlight = Highlight
pref-auto-type-underline = Underline
pref-auto-type-note = Note
pref-auto-type-text = Text
pref-auto-type-image = Area selection
pref-auto-item-types = Item categories (for example journalArticle, book; comma-separated)
pref-auto-filter-hint = Tags are matched against the annotation's tags; item categories against the type of the item the PDF belongs to. With everything empty, every new annotation is sent.
pref-auto-queue-retry = Retry the queue now
pref-auto-queue-clear = Clear the queue
pref-auto-queue-status = Pending queue: %d
pref-auto-queue-empty = The pending queue is empty
pref-auto-queue-retrying = Retrying…
pref-auto-queue-cleared = The pending queue was cleared
pref-auto-queue-left = %d could not be sent yet; they will be retried automatically
pref-auto-queue-sent = %d sent from the queue
pref-auto-queue-hint = When SiYuan is not running or a write fails, an automatically sent annotation goes into the pending queue. It is retried on the next start, and as soon as any send succeeds. Turning automatic sending off pauses the queue.

pref-picture-title = Pictures
pref-image-compress = Compress the picture before sending
pref-image-quality = Compression quality
pref-image-saved = Saved
pref-picture-hint = Area-selection screenshots and the pictures inside child notes are both compressed with these settings before they are sent. An area selection is a screenshot of the page, with an alpha channel that is completely opaque — several times as big as it needs to be; it is turned into a JPEG, which usually leaves about a fifth of it, and the original is kept when that is not smaller. The quality is yours to choose: the smaller the number, the smaller and rougher the picture; 100 is the biggest and the clearest.

